Subject: [PATCH 0/2] ALSA: hda: aw88399: Add per-model firmware loading

The AW88399 HDA side codec driver currently requests firmware
using the same hardcoded generic filename ("aw88399_acf.bin")
as the ASoC driver it was derived from.
This requires users to manually extract the firmware from the
Windows driver, rename it suitably, and place it in /lib/firmware.
This is not sustainable for distribution packaging.

This series adds support for per-model firmware filenames
based on the ACPI subsystem ID (e.g. "awinic/aw88399_acf_17aa3938.bin"),
making the driver compatible with the linux-firmware repository's
per-device naming convention.
Firmware submission to linux-firmware is in progress with AWINIC
and Lenovo.

Patch 1 adds a name parameter to the shared firmware request function
so callers can specify the filename.

Patch 2 uses the ACPI subsystem ID to construct model-specific firmware
names in the HDA driver.

Marco Giunta (2):
  ASoC: aw88399: pass firmware name as argument
  ALSA: hda: aw88399: use SSID-specific firmware name

